WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.352
The Jackson family are on holiday in Turkey.

00:00:04.412 --> 00:00:08.534
They are staying at a big hotel in Istanbul.

00:00:08.594 --> 00:00:16.549
Mark (13), his sister Fay (12), and their parents like Turkey.

00:00:16.609 --> 00:00:21.531
It is beautiful, the weather is hot, and the food is good.

00:00:21.592 --> 00:00:24.143
There is a lot to see, too.

00:00:24.203 --> 00:00:28.351
Today they are visiting the city of Troy.

00:00:28.411 --> 00:00:31.168
It is nine o’clock in the morning.

00:00:31.228 --> 00:00:36.591
They are getting on a bus in front of their hotel.

00:00:36.651 --> 00:00:40.882
There are forty people on the bus.

00:00:40.942 --> 00:00:49.817
They come from Britain, America, France, Italy and Holland.

00:00:49.877 --> 00:00:55.530
At Troy they all have lunch.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.728
Then they start to look at the old city.

00:00:58.788 --> 00:01:01.795
It's a very hot day.

00:01:01.855 --> 00:01:06.556
After an hour, Mark sits under a tree.

00:01:06.616 --> 00:01:09.918
I’m going to stop here for a moment,

00:01:09.978 --> 00:01:11.968
he tells Fay.

00:01:12.028 --> 00:01:15.320
OK, she answers.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:18.911
Then Mark sees something on the ground.

00:01:18.971 --> 00:01:22.613
What’s that? he thinks.
 
00:01:22.672 --> 00:01:26.054
It is a flat, yellow stone.

00:01:26.114 --> 00:01:28.192
Mark picks it up.

00:01:28.252 --> 00:01:32.082
Then he starts to clean it with his hands.

00:01:32.142 --> 00:01:36.866
But I know this stone, he thinks.

00:01:36.926 --> 00:01:44.270
It comes from ... from ... Suddenly there is a white light in his eyes.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:46.412
Mark closes them.

00:01:46.471 --> 00:01:48.563
The light is strong.

00:01:48.623 --> 00:01:51.685
Now there is a loud wind in his ears.

00:01:51.745 --> 00:01:55.528
He cannot hear or see anything.

00:01:55.588 --> 00:01:59.845
What’s happening? he thinks.
 
00:01:59.905 --> 00:02:04.588
Ten seconds later, the light and the wind stop.

00:02:04.648 --> 00:02:07.240
Mark opens his eyes.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.912
He is standing on a beach.

00:02:09.972 --> 00:02:13.654
He can see hundreds of ships and men.

00:02:13.714 --> 00:02:18.818
Behind him there is a beautiful city with high walls.

00:02:18.878 --> 00:02:22.621
Where am I? he thinks.
 
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.233
Where’s my family?

00:02:25.292 --> 00:02:28.924
He puts the yellow stone in his pocket.

00:02:28.984 --> 00:02:35.146
Then one of the men says to him, Boy! Come here!

00:02:35.206 --> 00:02:37.216
Me?

00:02:37.276 --> 00:02:41.898
Mark walks across the beach to a long, black ship.

00:02:41.958 --> 00:02:45.559
Carry this, the man says.

00:02:45.619 --> 00:02:48.330
He gives Mark a lot of wood.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.830
Then he gets off the ship.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:54.142
Follow me, he says.

00:02:54.202 --> 00:02:56.456
Mark follows him.

00:02:56.516 --> 00:03:01.542
The man is very tall and has a short, brown beard.

00:03:01.602 --> 00:03:05.283
I don’t know your face, he says.
 
00:03:05.343 --> 00:03:07.384
Are you new here?

00:03:07.444 --> 00:03:10.654
Y-yes, Mark answers.
 
00:03:10.714 --> 00:03:14.526
That’s right. I’m new here.
 
00:03:14.586 --> 00:03:19.696
My name is Andros, says the man.
 
00:03:19.756 --> 00:03:23.568
He and Mark walk for another ten minutes.

00:03:23.628 --> 00:03:26.519
Then they climb a small hill.

00:03:26.578 --> 00:03:29.710
At the top, Mark stops.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:35.070
There, in front of them, is a big wooden horse.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:39.301
Andros sees Mark's face and smiles.

00:03:39.361 --> 00:03:44.742
Well, what do you think of it? he asks.
 
00:03:44.802 --> 00:03:47.302
Mark doesn't answer.

00:03:47.362 --> 00:03:54.364
And Andros says, This horse is going to win the war for us Greeks.

00:03:54.424 --> 00:03:57.247
They walk down the hill.

00:03:57.307 --> 00:04:01.001
There are a lot of men working under the horse.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:04.021
One of them talks to Andros.

00:04:04.081 --> 00:04:07.472
There’s a problem, he says.

00:04:07.532 --> 00:04:10.912
We can’t find a stone for the second eye.

00:04:10.972 --> 00:04:14.493
We must find one before tomorrow.

00:04:14.553 --> 00:04:18.894
Mark looks at the horse's one bright eye.

00:04:18.954 --> 00:04:22.604
Then he remembers the stone in his pocket.

00:04:22.664 --> 00:04:25.145
Wait, he says.

00:04:25.205 --> 00:04:27.896
I think I can help you.

00:04:27.956 --> 00:04:31.658
He takes the stone out of his pocket.

00:04:31.718 --> 00:04:35.199
But how? says Andros.
 
00:04:35.259 --> 00:04:37.600
The man smiles.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:41.180
That’s it! That’s it!
 
00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.721
He looks at Mark.

00:04:43.781 --> 00:04:46.392
What’s your name, boy?

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.482
Mark tells him.

00:04:48.542 --> 00:04:52.454
He’s new here, says Andros.
 
00:04:52.513 --> 00:04:56.895
Ah! The man's very happy.
 
00:04:56.955 --> 00:05:00.641
Well, we must thank him.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.692
I know!

00:05:02.751 --> 00:05:07.274
You can come with us in the horse tomorrow night.

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:10.074
Mark's mouth opens.

00:05:10.134 --> 00:05:12.516
Me?

00:05:12.576 --> 00:05:18.358
That evening, Mark sits near a big fire on the beach.

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:21.199
There's an old woman beside him.

00:05:21.259 --> 00:05:25.030
Her name is Ana, and she is a cook.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:28.485
She tells Mark lots of stories.

00:05:28.545 --> 00:05:36.122
Stories about Greece, the war, and the beautiful princess, Helen.

00:05:36.182 --> 00:05:39.586
In the end, she goes to bed.

00:05:39.645 --> 00:05:43.388
Goodbye, boy, she says.
 
00:05:43.448 --> 00:05:46.310
Come and see me again one day.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:49.722
Come and see me again.

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:54.394
Next morning the horse is ready.

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:58.052
Greek soldiers pull it to the gates of Troy.

00:05:58.112 --> 00:06:00.439
Then they leave it there.

00:06:00.498 --> 00:06:04.391
Inside the horse there are forty Greeks.

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:09.194
They wait all afternoon under the hot yellow sun.

00:06:09.254 --> 00:06:12.566
Mark is sitting in the horse’s head.

00:06:12.626 --> 00:06:16.379
What happens now? he thinks.
 
00:06:16.438 --> 00:06:29.900
Suddenly the gates open.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:29.260
Trojan soldiers walk out.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:34.795
They pull the horse inside and shut the gates again.

00:06:34.855 --> 00:06:38.638
Mark can hear the Trojans.

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:42.422
Why are the Greeks giving us this horse?

00:06:42.482 --> 00:06:44.312
asks one.

00:06:44.372 --> 00:06:47.736
Do you think they want to end the war?

00:06:47.796 --> 00:06:50.498
Yes, look!

00:06:50.558 --> 00:06:54.080
says a soldier on top of the city walls.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:56.986
Their ships are leaving!

00:06:57.046 --> 00:07:04.852
After that, the Trojans eat, sing and dance all evening.

00:07:04.912 --> 00:07:12.054
Then they go to bed very late, and Troy is quiet.

00:07:12.114 --> 00:07:17.746
At that moment the Greeks climb out of the horse.

00:07:17.806 --> 00:07:22.077
Four men go to the gates and open them.

00:07:22.137 --> 00:07:27.393
A minute later, there are thousands of Greek soldiers in the city.

00:07:27.453 --> 00:07:30.891
They and their ships are back!

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:34.452
They run from one building to another.

00:07:34.512 --> 00:07:38.716
In five minutes, Troy is on fire.

00:07:38.776 --> 00:07:41.648
Mark watches all this.

00:07:41.708 --> 00:07:45.511
Suddenly, he sees a beautiful woman.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:48.814
She's running along the city walls.

00:07:48.874 --> 00:07:52.286
It’s Helen, he thinks.

00:07:52.345 --> 00:07:55.100
Helen of Troy!

00:07:55.160 --> 00:08:01.006
At that moment Andros says, Follow me, boy.

00:08:01.066 --> 00:08:05.208
He runs down a small street very fast.

00:08:05.268 --> 00:08:09.612
Mark follows, but the street is full of smoke.

00:08:09.672 --> 00:08:13.584
After a minute he cannot see anything.

00:08:13.644 --> 00:08:18.797
Andros! he says. Where are you?

00:08:18.856 --> 00:08:24.436
Then suddenly two Trojans with swords come out of the smoke.

00:08:24.496 --> 00:08:26.724
Mark looks at them.

00:08:26.784 --> 00:08:30.336
Please don’t kill me, he says.
 
00:08:30.395 --> 00:08:34.418
Don’t kill me! Please!
 
00:08:34.478 --> 00:08:38.401
Mark! Mark!
 
00:08:38.461 --> 00:08:40.282
It’s four o’clock.

00:08:40.342 --> 00:08:43.184
The bus is leaving in a minute.

00:08:43.244 --> 00:08:46.986
Fay is looking down at Mark.

00:08:47.046 --> 00:08:51.100
After a moment, he suddenly wakes up.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:54.082
What? he asks.
 
00:08:54.142 --> 00:08:58.605
The bus is leaving, Fay says again.

00:08:58.665 --> 00:09:02.517
Then she asks, Are you OK?

00:09:02.577 --> 00:09:04.728
Your face is white.

00:09:04.788 --> 00:09:07.710
And what’s that dirty stone?

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:11.592
Mark looks at the yellow stone in his hand.

00:09:11.652 --> 00:09:17.404
This? Oh ... it’s nothing, he says.
 
00:09:17.464 --> 00:09:20.106
Mark stands up.

00:09:20.166 --> 00:09:22.585
He sees an old woman.

00:09:22.645 --> 00:09:27.154
She has lots of small wooden horses in a basket.

00:09:27.214 --> 00:09:31.727
Do you want one, boy? she asks.
 
00:09:31.787 --> 00:09:34.818
Yes. Why not?
 
00:09:34.878 --> 00:09:39.090
Mark buys a horse and looks at the woman.

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:44.083
No. It can’t be, he thinks.
 
00:09:44.143 --> 00:09:46.714
He walks to the bus.

00:09:46.774 --> 00:09:50.916
Behind him, the old woman smiles.

00:09:50.976 --> 00:09:53.257
Goodbye, boy,

00:09:53.317 --> 00:09:57.935
she says. Come and see me again one day.

00:09:57.995 --> 00:10:00.159
Come and see me again.